  data:  # fa59
    kind: invariant  # fa59
    title: "python CFG: the else_clause of a try/for/while statement is never walked; its body is absent from the CFG, so def/use, DDG edges and the taint walk never see it (0.1-1.9% of Python functions forfeit)"  # fa59
    status: violated  # fa59
    priority: 3  # fa59
    parent:  # fa59
    tags:  # fa59
    - taint  # fa59
    - analysis_quality  # fa59
    - python  # fa59
    - ddg  # fa59
    isbefore: []  # fa59
    duplicate_of: []  # fa59
    not_duplicate_of: []  # fa59
    pr_ref:  # fa59
    description: "**Found 2026-11-04** during the sibling sweep that INV-kakav's own closure bar required (repeated-child shapes of Python compound statements), on the merged dev tree 1119eff00f. Multiple `except_clause`s are iterated by type (`cfg.py` `_process_try`, \"Find catch clauses by type\") and `match` arms are iterated over the `body` container (switch handler), both probed clean. The `else_clause` of `try`, `for` and `while` is a different gap: no mapping names it and no handler has a slot for it, so the whole clause is skipped.\n\n**Minimal repros** (`~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/kakav_fix_11042026/try_else_repro.py`, `loop_else_repro.py`, probe `probe_function.py FILE NAME`; results in `*_repro_merged_1119eff00f.txt`):\n\n```\ndef try_else(f, out):\n    try:\n        v = f()\n    except ValueError:\n        v = None\n    else:\n        out.append(v)   # line 7: uncovered\n    return out\n\ndef for_else(items, out):\n    for x in items:\n        if x:\n            break\n    else:\n        out.append(\"none\")   # line 6: uncovered\n    return out\n```\n\n`uncovered_semantic_lines` = {7} for `try_else`, {17} for `try_else_finally` (the `finally` body IS walked), {6} for `for_else`, {15} for `while_else`. `try_finally_only` is clean. The `for_statement` entry in `cfg_nodes/python.yaml` already says \"The `else:` clause is not processed by this hook\"; nothing in the tracker filed it (grep of the committed corpus for `else_clause` and try/else: no hit).\n\n**Root cause.** `cfg_nodes/python.yaml` `try_catch` names `body_child`, `catch_clause_type`, `finally_child` and nothing for the else clause; `loop` names `condition_child` / `body_child` and nothing for it either. `CfgBuilder` has no field for an else clause in either category, so the `else_clause` child is never visited: its statements are not in any block, `uncovered_semantic_lines` lists them, and the function lands in `RepoDdg.forfeit_refutation`. Python is the only shipped DDG grammar with these clauses (c, go, java, rust, typescript have no try-else or loop-else).\n\n**Blast radius** (`else_clause_census.py`, `else_clause_census.txt`; a function counts when a try/for/while in its body has an `else_clause` child):\n\n| tree | functions | with an else clause | by host |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| packages/hypergumbo-core/src | 3095 | 4 (0.1%) | try 1, for 3 |\n| packages/hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/src | 1556 | 3 (0.2%) | for 3, while 1 |\n| django/django | 9484 | 184 (1.9%) | try 176, for 23, while 2 |\n| httpx/httpx | 1134 | 4 (0.4%) | try 2, for 3 |\n\n**Consequences.** Same three as INV-kakav, smaller population: (1) the function forfeits refutation, every same-function sink reads approximate under ADR-0017 mixed mode; (2) definitions and uses inside the else body produce no DDG edges (a seed used only there reads `source_not_tracked`); (3) a definition in a try-else body cannot kill or reach anything, so a later use sees only the pre-try definition.\n\n**Fix shape (structural).** Add `else_child: \"type:else_clause\"` to the python `try_catch` and `loop` mappings and a matching field on `TryCatchMapping` / `LoopMapping`. Try: process the else clause as a partial on the no-exception path, entered from the try body's fringe only (not from any catch), and feed its fringe (plus the catch fringes) into `finally` / the join. Loops: the else partial is entered from the loop's condition-false / exhausted edge; `break` edges bypass it and go straight to the loop exit (the current fringe from `break` must NOT flow into the else entry). Pin with tests per host (try-else, try-else-finally, for-else with break, while-else with break) that assert the else body's lines are recorded and `uncovered_semantic_lines` is empty, and that a `break` path does not reach the else block. The five other grammars have no such clause; a mapping without `else_child` must take exactly today's path (pin one).\n\n**Pre-registered verification.** After the fix: the four repro functions have no uncovered lines; `for_else`'s else statement is reachable from the loop header's false edge and NOT from the `break` block; self-tree `forfeit_refutation` shrinks by the functions in the census that have no OTHER uncovered construct (core 2 -> expected ~0 beyond this family; measure with `measure_ddg.py` before/after, never totals); the self-claims gate stays at 23 `confirmed_with_caveats`. The general claim \"every clause of every Python compound statement is in the CFG\" is NOT asserted by this item; it covers the three `else_clause` hosts only."  # fa59
    fields:  # fa59
      statement: "Every else_clause of a Python try, for or while statement is a CFG branch: the try else body is on the no-exception path after the try body and before finally; the loop else body is on the loop's normal-exit edge (condition false or iterator exhausted) and is not reached from a break."  # fa59
      root_cause: "cfg_nodes/python.yaml names no else child for the try_catch or loop categories (the for_statement entry even says the else clause is not processed) and CfgBuilder's try and loop handlers have no slot for one, so the else_clause child is skipped: its statements are in no block, uncovered_semantic_lines lists them and the function lands in forfeit_refutation."  # fa59
